 "narrative": "The new reciprocal f027=1 estimates provide useful corroboration of the core marker pattern but remain sparse. H104 estimates feature_037=1 versus 0 within feature_027=1 at +0.785 [0.580, 0.990]; H105 estimates feature_010=1 versus 0 within feature_027=1 at +0.835 [0.598, 1.071]; H106 estimates feature_002=1 versus 0 within feature_027=1 at +0.668 [0.425, 0.910]. All lower bounds exceed the 0.15-unit threshold and the directions match the accepted core pattern: feature_037 and feature_027 mark stronger dependency, while feature_010 and feature_002 mark weaker dependency. However, the exposed cells are only 29, 24, and 29, respectively. I therefore accept these as dataset-specific conditional associations but defer them; they support the conclusion that the dominant markers are not mutually exclusive artifacts of the clean strata, but they should not be treated as central independent discoveries.\n\nThe median-split clinical-course estimates are stronger. In the high-log_pfs, f037=0/f010=0 stratum, feature_002 remains strongly associated with weaker dependency: H113 is +0.844 [0.784, 0.905] with exposed n=123. The parallel high-log_pfs estimates for feature_037 (H111, +0.802 [0.735, 0.869]) and feature_010 (H112, +0.803 [0.731, 0.875]) are also threshold-exceeding with adequate cells. I accept H111 and H112 as completed conditional corroboration and close them because the core marginal associations for feature_037 and feature_010 are already accepted and large. H113 is the only new conditional claim that is both adequately powered and plausibly susceptible to conditioning-induced selection artifacts, because it conditions on high log_pfs and on absence of two accepted marker directions. I accept it provisionally but leave it active and request independent validation. If validation remains threshold-exceeding, the high-log_pfs feature_002 conditional association becomes more stable; if it fails, the marginal feature_002 finding remains supported, but H113 itself would need to be weakened or unresolved.\n\nH110 tests feature_027 in the lower-log_pfs, triple-strong-absent stratum. It is +0.742 [0.639, 0.845] with exposed n=32, so it clears the threshold decisively despite the modest exposed cell. I accept it but defer it. It is consistent with the accepted validated feature_027 association and with the earlier high-log_pfs sparse estimate H97, but it remains a sparse conditional estimate and should not be elevated into a precise clinical-course-specific claim.\n\nThe broad probes and heterogeneity probe are negative. H103, feature_034 level_003 versus level_002, is near null: -0.012 [-0.150, 0.126]. H107, feature_047=1 versus 0, is +0.031 [-0.045, 0.107]. H108, feature_046 level_003 versus level_002, is -0.043 [-0.190, 0.103]. H109, feature_061 level_003 versus level_002, is -0.057 [-0.194, 0.080]. None provides evidence of a threshold-exceeding association in the claimed direction, so I reject and close these. H116 tests whether the feature_037 association is amplified when feature_038 is high. The interaction is +0.024 [-0.127, 0.176]; its upper bound alone touches the threshold, but the lower bound does not, so the evidence does not support a meaningful interaction. I reject and close it.\n\nOverall, these results strengthen the core dataset-specific pattern: feature_037=1 and feature_027=1 are associated with stronger composite dependency, feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 with weaker dependency, and the large marker associations persist in many reciprocal and clinical-course strata. The sparse f027=1 conditionals and the lower-log_pfs f027 estimate should remain deferred because of small exposed cells. The validation request for H113 is intended to test whether one adequately powered but heavily conditioned high-log_pfs association is stable outside the discovery subset. All accepted statements remain observational associations in this dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
 "research_notes": "Current core dataset-specific accepted pattern: f037=1 -> stronger dependency; f010=1 and f002=1 -> weaker dependency; f027=1 -> stronger dependency, validated in clean triple-strong-absent context and stable in broad/strict clean strata; f063=1 supported only in clean validated triple-strong-absent contexts, not broad/sparse/high-logpfs variants.\n\nNew corroboration: H104-H106 accept/defer; they show f037/f010/f002 associations persist within f027=1 but with exposed cells only 24-29, so they are corroboration not central discoveries. H110 accept/defer: f027 in lower-logpfs triple-absent is strong but exposed n=32. H111-H112 accept/close: high-logpfs f037/f010 in other-marker-absent strata are robust. H113 accept/active: high-logpfs f002 in f037=0/f010=0 is large and adequately powered; validation requested to guard against conditioning/selection artifacts.\n\nNegative/closed: H103 f034 level_003 vs level_002; H107 f047; H108 f046 level_003 vs level_002; H109 f061 level_003 vs level_002; H116 f037 interaction with f038>=0.75. H117 f037 interaction with f024 level_002 remains active/untested. H114-H115 strict f003-exclusion refinements of f063/f027 remain near-threshold/mining; not prioritized.\n\nNext plan: run H117 if active capacity remains. Do not further chase f003 or broad/sparse f063. For future proposals, prefer adequate-cell broad comparisons with pre-specified directions and accept only if lower bound clearly exceeds 0.15. Preserve validation for new threshold-ambiguous or selection-sensitive robustness claims. All conclusions remain observational in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable.",
