  "narrative": "The two due validations strengthen the already coherent core pattern and do not change the substantive conclusions. For H83, feature_027=1 versus 0 in the clean stratum feature_037=0, feature_010=0, and feature_002=0 gives discovery +0.745 [0.666, 0.825] and independent validation +0.779 [0.675, 0.884]. Both signed lower bounds are far above the 0.15-unit threshold, so the association of feature_027=1 with stronger composite dependency is robust in this clean context. I keep H83 accepted and closed. For H113, feature_002=1 versus 0 in the higher-log_pfs stratum with feature_037=0 and feature_010=0 gives discovery +0.844 [0.784, 0.905] and independent validation +0.804 [0.704, 0.903]. Because the hypothesis direction is +1, this signed positive estimate corresponds to feature_002=1 being associated with the claimed direction for that predictor, i.e. weaker composite dependency, and the independent lower bound remains well above threshold. I accept H113 and close it as a dataset-specific conditional robustness result. These validations reduce concern that the dominant-marker associations are artifacts of one stratum or selection in the high-log_pfs conditional. They do not support causal interpretation or generalization beyond the supplied dataset. The main supported pattern remains: feature_037=1 and feature_027=1 are associated with stronger composite dependency, while feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 are associated with weaker dependency. feature_063 remains supported primarily in the clean validated triple-strong-absent context and narrowly bounded clean conditionals; broad or sparse feature_063 variants remain unresolved. feature_003 remains near-threshold and unresolved. Negative findings include the research markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 in marginal and tested signature/subgroup contrasts, feature_017, many low-prevalence binary markers, several nominal categorical contrasts, feature_034 level contrasts tested, feature_047, feature_046 level_003 versus level_002, feature_061 level_003 versus level_002, feature_053 value contrast, and the tested heterogeneity interactions of feature_037 with feature_010, feature_002, feature_040 median split, and feature_038 high threshold, plus feature_027 interactions with feature_037, feature_010, and feature_002. The most informative next analysis is to run the registered feature_037-by-feature_024 interaction probe H117 and avoid further feature_063 or feature_003 refinement unless a comparison has clearly adequate cells and a strong rationale. Sparse deferred claims such as H104-H106 and H110 should remain low-confidence corroboration rather than central discoveries.",
  "research_notes": "Core dataset-specific accepted pattern updated: f037=1 -> stronger dependency; f010=1 and f002=1 -> weaker dependency; f027=1 -> stronger dependency. H83 remains accepted/closed after validation R91 (+0.779 [0.675,0.884]) in clean triple-strong-absent f037/f010/f002 stratum. H113 now accepted/closed after validation R118 (+0.804 [0.704,0.903]) for f002 in high-logpfs f037=0/f010=0 stratum. This confirms dominant markers are not conditional artifacts of that selection. f063 remains bounded: accepted validated H55 and clean excluding f027 H89, plus non-sparse H52/H69; broad/sparse/high-logpfs variants unresolved. f003 remains unresolved near-threshold. Negative/closed: H7, H29, H103, H107, H108, H109, H116, many low-prevalence binaries and categorical probes. Next analyze: prioritize registered H117 (f037 interaction with f024 level_002). Consider H114/H115 only if cell adequacy is clear; do not chase them if sparse. Preserve validation capacity for genuinely new threshold-exceeding robustness questions, not near-threshold refinements. All claims are observational associations in this dataset, not causal or generalizable effects."
